{
  "track": "es",
  "level": "A2",
  "unit": 1,
  "title": "Things you do",
  "description": "Say what you eat, drink, read, and learn.",
  "explanation": {
    "summary": "The -er verbs follow exactly the same pattern as the -ar verbs, with two endings changed. Once you know the -ar pattern, the -er pattern is a two-minute job.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "The six endings",
        "body": "Drop the -er and add -o, -es, -e, -emos, -éis, -en. Comer becomes como, comes, come, comemos, coméis, comen. Compare with the -ar pattern: the endings are -o, -as, -a, -amos, -áis, -an. Only the second and third endings differ.",
        "examples": [
          {
            "es": "Como verduras.",
            "en": "I eat vegetables."
          },
          {
            "es": "¿Dónde vives?",
            "en": "Where do you live?"
          },
          {
            "es": "Aprendemos español juntos.",
            "en": "We learn Spanish together."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "A spelling change to watch",
        "body": "A few -er verbs change their stem in the yo form. Querer becomes quiero, poder becomes puedo, and the -er verbs with a yo ending in -go are irregular: venir becomes vengo, decir becomes digo. Learn the yo form separately from the rest.",
        "examples": [
          {
            "es": "Quiero aprender más.",
            "en": "I want to learn more."
          },
          {
            "es": "No puedo venir hoy.",
            "en": "I cannot come today."
          },
          {
            "es": "Leo el libro en la mesa.",
            "en": "I read the book at the table."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "Before and after",
        "body": "Some verbs take a preposition, and it is fixed: hablar con, hablar de, soñar con, depender de. The preposition goes before the infinitive: hablo con Ana, sueño con la casa. The order is subject, verb, preposition, infinitive.",
        "examples": [
          {
            "es": "Hablamos con el profesor.",
            "en": "We spoke with the teacher."
          },
          {
            "es": "Sueño con viajar.",
            "en": "I dream of travelling."
          },
          {
            "es": "Depende del tiempo.",
            "en": "It depends on the weather."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
